# Configuration for slurm/train_gan.sh 128, read when the job starts.
#
# History:
# 1. Hinge loss, spectral normalisation, translation and cutout DiffAugment
#    collapsed in the smoke test, job 590977: by step 1,000 all 64 progress
#    samples were one brain.
# 2. slurm/sweep_gan.sh then compared four configurations at 64x64 for 2,500
#    steps. The diversity ratio (generated / real) at each 500-step sample:
#
#      a  hinge + spectral norm, translation         2.00 1.02 0.44 0.22 0.14 0.09
#      b  logistic + R1 gamma 1, translation         1.68 0.72 0.32 0.35 0.23 0.21
#      c  logistic + R1 gamma 10, translation        1.96 0.93 0.42 0.16 0.08 0.06
#      d  logistic + R1 gamma 10, no augmentation    1.52 1.00 0.69 0.79 0.93 0.94
#
#    Every run with augmentation collapsed; the one without recovered. This is
#    configuration d. The sweep did not include hinge with spectral norm and no
#    augmentation, so it shows d works, not that R1 beats spectral normalisation.
#
# --diffaugment= passes an empty policy as a single word; a quoted "" would
# reach Python as two quote characters, because this file is split on spaces.
--loss logistic
--r1-gamma 10
--no-spectral-norm
--diffaugment=
--lr-g 2e-4
--lr-d 2e-4
--beta2 0.99
#
# 3. The first long run with this configuration (job 591530) was healthy from
#    step 3,000 to 10,000 (diversity 0.79-0.92), then collapsed: 0.52 at 11,000,
#    0.10 by 14,000. It was cancelled. train_gan.py's collapse rule (defaults:
#    snapshot at ratio >= 0.8, stop below 0.6 twice in a row, from step 5,000)
#    now keeps the last healthy generator as final.pt.
